86157494 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186158162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157494 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186158163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157494 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186158164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157494 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186158168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157494 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186158171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157494 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157494 #edb/ref 1045 "Modeling With the Geometric Distribution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157494 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186158168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157494 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157494 #edb/ref 1050 720.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157494 #edb/ref 1050 720.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186157494 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "4e86130c-1f86-5c43-8ce5-5c7ae15aaad2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157868 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186156129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157868 #edb/ref 1069 "q-85277" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157868 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157868 #edb/ref 1071 "At a water bottle factory, every batch of $1\\,000$ water bottles has $20$ water bottles (on average) on which the label is upside down. If an inspector comes to inspect the water bottles, what is the probability that they will find an upside down label before checking the $5$th bottle? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157868 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1c241a6a-1a9e-5d8e-adf5-2fd9b0826eb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157868 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157868 #edb/ref 1074 "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of bottles checked until a defect is found. On average, the chance of finding an upside down label on any water bottle is \n\n$$\np=\\frac{20}{1\\,000}=0.02.\n$$\n\nSo, the number of bottles that the inspector checks before finding an upside down label can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success $p=0.02.$\n\nSo, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.02).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(1-0.02)^{x-1}(0.02) \\\\  & =(0.98)^{x-1}(0.02)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability of finding an upside down label before checking the $5$th bottle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =(0.98)^{1-1}(0.02)+(0.98)^{2-1}(0.02)+(0.98)^{3-1}(0.02)+(0.98)^{4-1}(0.02) \\\\  & =(0.02)+(0.98)(0.02)+(0.98)^{2}(0.02)+(0.98)^{3}(0.02) \\\\  & =[1+0.98+(0.98)^{2}+(0.98)^{3}](0.02) \\\\  & ≈0.078\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158161 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158161 #edb/ref 1061 27844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158161 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1fa58b97-b6b2-5edd-8734-614f560a7651" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158161 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158162 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158162 #edb/ref 1061 27845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158162 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22e52493-867b-5374-829e-6bc8df9e2158" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158162 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158163 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158163 #edb/ref 1061 27846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158163 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7a7fc129-73fd-5136-a99a-5948c4181281" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158163 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158164 #edb/ref 1061 27847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158164 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "23f94e12-bb19-5644-a2f6-54b67243d945